# The llama.cpp pins, one b-build per host class, and the repository of ggml's images. A class's
# build serves each of its flavors: host/llama.sh names the server image server-<flavor>-<build> in
# LLAMA_REPOSITORY, and llama_pin (host/llama-release.sh) reads the class's pin. LLAMA_RELEASE is
# the semver release last pinned, v0.8.0, whose notes ("Nightly build:") name b11960; neither class
# runs it now. gb10 (gb10-1; cuda13) runs b12098, the 2026-11-04 nightly image, which
# spike-hosting-upgrades' screen adopted (docs/screens/gb10-1/2026-11-05.md; the engine rule rolled
# it back and the architect overruled it). strix-halo (the Framework; rocm and vulkan) runs the
# same build, b12098, which spike-model-layout's hosts task moved it to on 2026-11-09. Both classes
# are held there: llama.cpp #31620 and #31639 (b12100 and later) match an -hf quantization tag only
# after `-`, `.` or `/`, and Google's 26B-A4B, 31B and E4B QAT GGUFs (such as
# gemma-4-26B_q4_0-it.gguf) put `_` before it, so their sections don't resolve on them (the 12B's,
# gemma-4-12b-it-qat-q4_0.gguf, puts `-` there and still resolves); checked still unrestored
# through b12271. Revisit when Google renames its QAT GGUFs or llama.cpp accepts `_`. The
# Framework's re-screen of Gemma 4 26B-A4B waits on llama.cpp #25584, the fix for #29221 (Vulkan's
# "tensor not allocated" abort on a 15-slot section's second request), and #31418 (Vulkan's
# batched tensor copy API) (spike-hosting-upgrades, docs/screens/framework/2026-11-04.md and
# docs/screens/gb10-1/2026-11-05.md). So currency reports both classes behind. scripts/currency.sh
# compares each class's pin with the newest b-build that has the class's server image on ghcr.io,
# not with LLAMA_RELEASE's build. Sourced by host/llama-release.sh.
LLAMA_RELEASE=v0.8.0
LLAMA_BUILD_GB10=b12098
LLAMA_BUILD_STRIX_HALO=b12098
LLAMA_REPOSITORY=ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp
